sequenceDiagram
  participant C as Round instruments
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  participant T as Target
  participant Z as Zabbix
  participant P as Polaris API/engine/executor
  participant W as Web interface
  actor H as Operator
  C->>D: Persist and commit t0 before injection
  C->>C: Arm independent observer
  C->>T: Explicit administrative fault injection
  par Operational handling
  Z->>T: Monitor target
  Z-->>P: Event carrying detection time t1
  Note over Z,P: Webhook or reconciler recovery, global idempotency
  P->>D: Persist incident and explanation (t2)
  H->>W: Select incident and inspect suggestion
  W->>P: Read detail and record display
  P->>D: Persist first display (t3)
  alt Operator approves
    H->>W: Approve action and script version
    W->>P: Submit explicit decision
    P->>D: Persist approval, hash and t4, COMMIT
    P->>D: Reread approval before executor
    P->>T: Send allowed action or central script over privileged SSH
    P->>T: Verify health without sudo
    P->>D: Record operational outcome
    W->>P: Read result
    P-->>W: Execution and verification result
  else Operator rejects
    H->>W: Reject and provide reason
    W->>P: Submit rejection
    P->>D: Persist false decision and reason
    Note over P,T: Rejection never reaches executor
  end
  and Independent observation
  alt Observed fault and confirmed recovery
    C->>T: Apply common health criteria in both arms
    C->>D: Persist independent t5 of first qualifying sample
  else Missing or invalid measurement
    Note over C,D: Never invent t5, require assessment or explicit discard
  end
  end
  H->>C: Record actual steps and assessment, preserve evidence
  Note over D,P: Operational ts_conclusao does not replace round t5
